.TH WPDCS 1 "September 2026" "WPDCS 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wpdcs \- code style, doctests and documentation toolchain for Perl and Clojure
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wpdcs
[\fB\-\-json\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
WPDCS enforces a comment-tag standard (\fB##\fR for Perl, \fB;;\fR for Clojure),
runs executable examples as doctests, and generates Markdown documentation.
Paths may be files or directories (scanned recursively, minus
.B exclude_dirs
from \fI.wpdcsrc\fR).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B parse \fIPATH\fR...
Print all WPDCS tags with line numbers.
.TP
.B check \fIPATH\fR...
Validate required header tags; report missing, malformed, duplicate and unknown tags.
.TP
.B lint \fIPATH\fR...
Check style: trailing whitespace, tabs, CRLF, line length, tag format, EOF newline.
.TP
.B format \fIPATH\fR...
Rewrite files in place: strip trailing whitespace, expand tabs, ensure EOF newline.
.TP
.B docs \fIPATH\fR...
Generate Markdown documentation next to each source file.
.TP
.B test \fIPATH\fR...
Run \fB@ex\fR examples as doctests (Perl only; Clojure files are reported and skipped).
.TP
.B stats \fIPATH\fR...
Show tag counts, documentation coverage and doctest totals per file.
.TP
.B init [\fIDIR\fR]
Create \fI.wpdcsrc\fR, \fIexamples/\fR, \fIt/\fR, \fIdocs/\fR.
.TP
.B create \fINAME\fR
Create a new cargo-like project skeleton.
.TP
.B gen header \fIPATH\fR...
Prepend the WPDCS file header (preserves \fB#!\fR shebang).
.TP
.B gen funcinfo \fIPATH\fR...
Insert \fB@funcinfo\fR + \fB@param\fR + \fB@return\fR skeletons before undocumented functions.
.TP
.B gen test \fIFILE\fR
Generate a \fI.t\fR skeleton from the file's \fB@ex\fR doctests.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.TP
.B help [\fICOMMAND\fR]
Show help, optionally for one command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON output (parse, check, lint, test, stats, version).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .wpdcsrc
Project configuration: language, required_tags, exclude_dirs. See \fI.wpdcsrc.example\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; non-zero when any file fails the requested check.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR perl (1),
